:"Yes: \"If the route was changed while the driver was offline, the driver is shown the difference before continuing, and a handover already completed offline is never lost or undone.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-23","question":"Does the request ask for this: When an assigned route changes while a driver is offline, show route differences, require review and resolution of affected unsent work before continuing, and preserve completed offline handovers."},{"answer":"Yes: \"The system shows the reviewer the full temperature history, the budget used and remaining per tier, and a recommendation: Release when every tier still has allowance left, Reject when any tier is used up or a not-permitted range was reached.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-24","question":"Does the request ask for this: Present a single-person quality-decision flow only when an excursion is within the first tier above or below the permitted band, allowance remains, and the proposed decision matches the recommendation. Otherwise require a Quality Officer proposal and separate approval by a different Quality Manager. Require written justification when a decision opposes the recommendation."},{"answer":"Yes: \"Each decision is signed electronically: the person confirms their identity again at the moment of signing and gives a reason. A signed decision cannot be edited. It can only be superseded by a new signed decision, and both remain on record.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-25","question":"Does the request ask for this: Require identity confirmation using the account’s sign-in method and a reason when a user signs a quality decision; present signed decisions as read-only with a separate superseding-decision action."},{"answer":"Yes: \"If the excursion stayed within the first tier above or below the band and allowance remains, a Quality Officer may decide alone.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-26","question":"Does the request ask for this: When the service returns a quality disposition, show resulting stock, order, and route status and, when superseded, the earlier and current disposition."},{"answer":"Yes: \"Destruction is recorded with a date, a quantity and a witness.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-27","question":"Does the request ask for this: Collect destruction date, quantity, and witness for rejected stock, and prevent entry of a quantity greater than the displayed rejected quantity."},{"answer":"Yes: \"Decisions waiting longer than 4 hours are escalated to the Quality Manager.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-28","question":"Does the request ask for this: Identify decisions waiting more than four hours as escalated in the Quality Manager’s waiting-decisions view."},{"answer":"Yes: \"A Quality Manager starts a recall for a product and one or more lot numbers, with a reason and a severity.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-29","question":"Does the request ask for this: Provide a Quality Manager flow to start and close recalls with signed actions; recall start collects product, one or more lots, reason, and severity, and the app displays each returned action result."},{"answer":"Yes: \"The trace from lot to every location and customer shall be available within one minute of the request.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-30","question":"Does the request ask for this: Display the returned recall trace, including warehouse locations, boxes, routes, customer deliveries, quantities, delivery dates, receivers, and the trace total alongside received quantity when supplied."},{"answer":"Yes: \"Notifies those customers by email and in the customer portal.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-31","question":"Does the request ask for this: Show customer recall notices in the portal, link notices to affected deliveries, and provide a response entry point."},{"answer":"Yes: \"The customer portal shows the organisation's orders, their status, the lots and expiry dates allocated, and for deliveries on the road the planned arrival time and whether the temperature is in range.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-32","question":"Does the request ask for this: Show customers only their organisation’s current and past orders, allocated lots and expiry dates, order status, and in-transit delivery arrival and temperature status, without exposing other route customers."},{"answer":"Yes: \"After delivery, the customer can download a delivery certificate as a PDF for each delivery.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-33","question":"Does the request ask for this: Provide a PDF certificate for each completed delivery in the signed-in customer’s organisation, containing products, lots, expiry dates, quantities, receiver, handover time, each box’s temperature chart from sealing to handover, excursions, and signed excursion decisions."},{"answer":"Yes: \"Each affected customer responds in the portal with, for each delivery, how many packs are still on hand, how many were used or dispensed, and how many were destroyed on site.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-34","question":"Does the request ask for this: When late readings produce a new certificate version, list the new and earlier versions for the signed-in customer’s completed delivery and keep each available for download."},{"answer":"Yes: \"Recall progress shows the percentage of packs accounted for.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-35","question":"Does the request ask for this: Present the customer portal and certificates in the user’s selected English or Arabic, render Arabic right to left including tables and charts, and show dates and times in the account’s configured time zone."},{"answer":"Yes: \"A customer sees current and past orders of their own organisation only.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-36","question":"Does the request ask for this: Provide an audit-trail screen showing returned entries with actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and supplied reason; support filters by record, user, date range, and action type, and export the filtered view."},{"answer":"Yes: \"The certificate contains the contents by lot, the handover details, the temperature chart, and any excursions with their decisions.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-37","question":"Does the request ask for this: Show the returned history of a lot from receipt through delivery or destruction in time order."},{"answer":"Yes: \"The same figures shall be available on screen for any date range, filterable by warehouse.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-38","question":"Does the request ask for this: Provide on-screen reports for selected date ranges and warehouses, with CSV export of displayed figures, covering excursion counts and rates by route, driver, vehicle, and shipper box type; packs rejected and destroyed by product and cause; on-time deliveries within 60 minutes of planned arrival and in-full deliveries when every ordered pack is handed over, each as a percentage; average time from excursion to decision; stock within 60 days of expiry by product and warehouse; and open recalls and their progress."},{"answer":"Yes: \"The portal and the certificate are available in English and Arabic according to the user's preference.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-39","question":"Does the request ask for this: Make the web app responsive on phone, tablet, and desktop browsers, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens."},{"answer":"Yes: \"The trace lists every warehouse location, box, route and customer delivery for the lot, with quantities.\"","by":"factory","id":"Q-40","question":"Does the request ask for this: Render the full recall trace returned by the service for the assumed launch scale."}],"asked":[{"category":"errors","id":"Q-9","impact":2,"impactReason":"This affects delivery planning and sequencing, not product behavior.","options":["Approve all 34 requirements as one run.","Split the work into about three runs without cutting requirements.","Reject the scope and identify requirements to cut."],"reason":"This preserves the requested scope while addressing the estimate that it is about three runs of work.","recommended":"Split the work into about three runs without cutting requirements.","score":6,"spans":[],"text":"Should this 34-requirement scope be approved as one run, split into multiple runs, or reduced?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"errors","id":"Q-10","impact":3,"impactReason":"This affects who may create and send delivery records.","options":["Allow local recording after expiry, but require the driver to re-authenticate before queued work can sync.","Stop new recording when the session expires; retain previously queued work for syncing after re-authentication.","Allow recording and syncing without re-authentication until the browser is back online."],"reason":"This lets the driver continue the requested offline work while retaining the spec's re-authentication-before-sync rule.","recommended":"Allow local recording after expiry, but require the driver to re-authenticate before queued work can sync.","score":9,"spans":[],"text":"If a driver's session expires while the browser is offline, may the driver continue recording loading, handover, and refusal work?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"scope","id":"Q-11","impact":3,"impactReason":"This determines whether a handover is blocked and how a potentially recalled delivery is recorded.","options":["Apply recall blocks from the service while online; do not add offline-cache recall blocking or a separate recall-conflict quality-case flow.","Also block using cached recall information offline, and flag the handover and show the returned quality-case result if it conflicts with a recall during sync."],"reason":"The request requires the driver to see a recall block when online, but does not ask for offline-cache recall handling.","recommended":"Apply recall blocks from the service while online; do not add offline-cache recall blocking or a separate recall-conflict quality-case flow.","score":9,"spans":[],"text":"Should recall blocking and conflict handling extend to offline cached recall information, or apply only once the service is reachable? The request separately requires retaining and flagging an offline handover that conflicts with a hold.","uncertainty":3},{"category":"scope","id":"Q-12","impact":3,"impactReason":"This affects whether a delivery record can be completed and what location data it contains.","options":["Allow the handover and record the location as unavailable.","Require location to be available before completing the handover."],"reason":"This avoids blocking an otherwise valid handover when browser location is unavailable.","recommended":"Allow the handover and record the location as unavailable.","score":9,"spans":[],"text":"If the browser denies or cannot provide location, should an otherwise eligible handover still be allowed?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"scope","id":"Q-13","impact":3,"impactReason":"These rules govern who can see or send queued records and when delivery data is cleared or retried.","options":["Keep the requested offline queue and automatic sending, without adding the extra account-isolation and rejected-payload review rules.","Add the full safeguards: isolate queued work by account, require its originator to re-authenticate, preserve retry identifiers and occurrence times, retain payloads until acknowledgement, and require review before retrying permanent failures."],"reason":"The request asks for offline work to be sent automatically, but does not specify these additional queue policies.","recommended":"Keep the requested offline queue and automatic sending, without adding the extra account-isolation and rejected-payload review rules.","score":9,"spans":[],"text":"Should the offline queue include safeguards beyond the requested local work retention and automatic sending, such as account isolation, re-authentication, retry identifiers, and review of permanently rejected payloads?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"scope","id":"Q-14","impact":2,"impactReason":"This affects the visible compatibility target across browsers.","options":["Add support for the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.","Do not add a fixed browser-version support requirement."],"reason":"The request does not specify a browser-version matrix, so adding one would expand the acceptance scope.","recommended":"Do not add a fixed browser-version support requirement.","score":6,"spans":[],"text":"Should the web app have a formal browser support requirement for the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"scope","id":"Q-15","impact":2,"impactReason":"This affects design and testing expectations for the app's user-facing flows.","options":["Require the main web-app flows to conform to WCAG 2.1 AA.","Do not add a formal WCAG 2.1 AA requirement."],"reason":"Accessibility conformance is not specified in the request, so the recommendation avoids adding a new acceptance criterion.","recommended":"Do not add a formal WCAG 2.1 AA requirement.","score":6,"spans":[],"text":"Should WCAG 2.1 AA conformance be added as an acceptance requirement for the main flows?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"scope","id":"Q-16","impact":2,"impactReason":"This affects performance expectations and the scale against which the web client is assessed.","options":["Define and include a first-year product scale target.","Do not add a first-year product scale target; retain the explicitly requested lot-trace timing."],"reason":"The request specifies trace contents and timing but does not set a product-volume target.","recommended":"Do not add a first-year product scale target; retain the explicitly requested lot-trace timing.","score":6,"spans":[],"text":"Should a first-year product scale target be defined in this scope, in addition to the requested one-minute lot-trace availability?","uncertainty":3}],"checks":{"critic":[{"finding":"NFR-4 starts the 60-second trace budget when the response is received, but NFR-5 starts it at the user's request, so the two targets measure different intervals for the same screen and cannot both define pass/fail.","reqId":"NFR-4","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-18.2 adds a service rejection of superseding dispositions after delivery or destruction, but ASM-1 says the superseding decision is applied to stock and order/route state even when it reverses the earlier one.","reqId":"REQ-18","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-24.3 accepts 'a validation error or returned error message' and also 'sends no invalid response request', but a returned error can only exist after a request is sent, so it is unclear whether client-side blocking is required.","reqId":"REQ-24","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-12 retains work across session expiry but requires re-authentication before sync, and nothing says whether a driver whose session expires while offline can keep recording work, given that password checks need the service.","reqId":"REQ-12","rubric":2,"severity":"high"},{"finding":"No requirement or AC covers cold-starting or reloading the app while offline (cached app shell and cached route data), yet AC-12.1, AC-8.2 and AC-6.2 all assume the driver screens open with no connection.","reqId":"REQ-12","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Queued work is released only when the originating account re-authenticates, and no path is defined for work whose owner has been deactivated by the System Administrator (REQ-2), so that delivery evidence could stay stuck forever on the device.","reqId":"REQ-12","rubric":6,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-10 covers a denied location prompt, but no requirement covers a denied camera permission, a failed photo capture or an empty signature, even though the photo and signature are mandatory for a handover.","reqId":"REQ-9","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-11 requires a reason for each refused box, but no AC checks that submitting a refused box without a reason is blocked with a validation error.","reqId":"REQ-11","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-8 covers an offline cached Recalled status, but REQ-7 (On Hold) only uses the returned status and says nothing about offline holds, and neither says what happens when a scanned box has no cached status at all.","reqId":"REQ-7","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"No AC covers a failed identity confirmation (wrong password) or cancelling while signing a quality decision, recall action or write-off.","reqId":"REQ-17","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-15.2 refers to a 'settings' view of tier limits and allowances, but no requirement says who can view or edit this configuration, what the screen shows, or what happens if no tier configuration exists.","reqId":"REQ-15","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"ASM-16 asked what happens when the user's time zone is not set and answered circularly with the account's configured time zone, so REQ-29 still has no fallback for an account with no time zone.","reqId":"REQ-29","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Q-3 lets the remainder be either accounted for later or written off, but nothing defines what happens when a customer updates quantities (REQ-24) after a write-off or after the recall is closed.","reqId":"REQ-25","rubric":6,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Opening-inventory entry has no lifecycle, so after launch it stays a permanent way to create lots and stock without receipt, with no rule for when or how it is closed.","reqId":"REQ-33","rubric":6,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The dispatcher route-monitoring view has no permission or warehouse-scope path, although Q-2 scopes staff by assigned warehouses and REQ-32 checks scope only for reports.","reqId":"REQ-5","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"AC-26.1 assumes a customer user belongs to exactly one organisation, but Q-2 lets the administrator assign customer-organisation access, and no organisation switching or multi-organisation case is defined.","reqId":"REQ-26","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"No path covers a completed delivery whose certificate is not yet generated or available, and no accessibility target is set for the PDF, although ASM-6 asked specifically about generated customer certificates.","reqId":"REQ-27","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"There is no empty state for a driver with no routes today, and 'today' is not tied to any time zone.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"No empty or partial trace path is defined, for example a lot never shipped or a trace response that fails.","reqId":"REQ-22","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"No path covers the gateway feed being unavailable while the browser is online, and the age at which data counts as stale is not defined.","reqId":"REQ-6","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The 60-minute on-time window and the 60-day expiry horizon are fixed in the requirement text when they look like operational thresholds that should be configurable.","reqId":"REQ-32","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The four-hour escalation threshold is fixed in the requirement text instead of being treated as a configured value.","reqId":"REQ-20","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"REQ-8 cites Q-3, which is about recall-response quantities and does not support blocking handover of Recalled boxes, so the requirement is mis-anchored.","reqId":"REQ-8","rubric":5,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The rule that late readings produce new certificate versions is anchored only to Q-4 (evidence retention) and ASM-18 (accessibility), and neither supports it.","reqId":"REQ-28","rubric":5,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The full set of roles (Driver, Dispatcher, Quality Officer, Quality Manager, Auditor, staff, Customer) used across the spec is never defined for the administrator's assignment screen, and AC-2.2 lets 'page not displayed' pass without a clear denial.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The NFR text promises browser support for the whole app, but the metric tests only the driver and customer flows, leaving quality, audit, admin and reports screens unchecked.",