e signed-in customer’s organisation, containing products, lots, expiry dates, quantities, receiver, handover time, each box’s temperature chart from sealing to handover, excursions, and signed excursion decisions."},{"kind":"invented","text":"When late readings produce a new certificate version, list the new and earlier versions for the signed-in customer’s completed delivery and keep each available for download."},{"kind":"invented","text":"Present the customer portal and certificates in the user’s selected English or Arabic, render Arabic right to left including tables and charts, and show dates and times in the account’s configured time zone."},{"kind":"invented","text":"Provide an audit-trail screen showing returned entries with actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and supplied reason; support filters by record, user, date range, and action type, and export the filtered view."},{"kind":"invented","text":"Show the returned history of a lot from receipt through delivery or destruction in time order."},{"kind":"invented","text":"Provide on-screen reports for selected date ranges and warehouses, with CSV export of displayed figures, covering excursion counts and rates by route, driver, vehicle, and shipper box type; packs rejected and destroyed by product and cause; on-time deliveries within 60 minutes of planned arrival and in-full deliveries when every ordered pack is handed over, each as a percentage; average time from excursion to decision; stock within 60 days of expiry by product and warehouse; and open recalls and their progress."},{"kind":"invented","text":"Make the web app responsive on phone, tablet, and desktop browsers, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens."},{"kind":"invented","text":"Support the latest two browser versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox."},{"kind":"invented","text":"Conform the main web-app flows to WCAG 2.1 AA."},{"kind":"invented","text":"Render the full recall trace returned by the service for the assumed launch scale."},{"kind":"invented","text":"Support the assumed first-year product scale and make a requested lot trace available through its screen within the requested time limit."}],"round":1,"settled":[{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"The driver sees today's route with its stops in order.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Show drivers only their assigned routes for today, with each route’s stops in route order.","ref":"Q-17"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"Loading requires every box on the route to be scanned, and a wrong or missing box is reported.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Compare scanned shipper boxes with expected boxes before departure, report missing or wrong-route boxes, and block departure until every expected box is scanned and wrong boxes are removed or corrected.","ref":"Q-18"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"The dispatcher sees each stop's status and the time it was last updated.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Show dispatchers each route stop’s status and last-updated time.","ref":"Q-19"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"During the route the application shows the current temperature and status of each box and any alerts.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Show each route box’s latest available temperature, status, and gateway alerts, and mark cached temperature data as stale while disconnected.","ref":"Q-20"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"If a box holds stock that is On Hold, the application shows \"Do not deliver\" for that box and does not allow it to be handed over.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"For scanned boxes on hold, display “Do not deliver” and the returned hold reason, and prevent handover of those boxes.","ref":"Q-21"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"For the remaining boxes, the driver records the receiver's name, captures their signature and a photo of the delivered boxes, and completes the handover. The time and location are recorded automatically.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Let drivers record eligible handovers with receiver name, signature, delivery photo, actual handover time, and available browser location.","ref":"Q-22"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"If the route was changed while the driver was offline, the driver is shown the difference before continuing, and a handover already completed offline is never lost or undone.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"When an assigned route changes while a driver is offline, show route differences, require review and resolution of affected unsent work before continuing, and preserve completed offline handovers.","ref":"Q-23"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"The system shows the reviewer the full temperature history, the budget used and remaining per tier, and a recommendation: Release when every tier still has allowance left, Reject when any tier is used up or a not-permitted range was reached.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Present a single-person quality-decision flow only when an excursion is within the first tier above or below the permitted band, allowance remains, and the proposed decision matches the recommendation. Otherwise require a Quality Officer proposal and separate approval by a different Quality Manager. Require written justification when a decision opposes the recommendation.","ref":"Q-24"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"Each decision is signed electronically: the person confirms their identity again at the moment of signing and gives a reason. A signed decision cannot be edited. It can only be superseded by a new signed decision, and both remain on record.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Require identity confirmation using the account’s sign-in method and a reason when a user signs a quality decision; present signed decisions as read-only with a separate superseding-decision action.","ref":"Q-25"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"If the excursion stayed within the first tier above or below the band and allowance remains, a Quality Officer may decide alone.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"When the service returns a quality disposition, show resulting stock, order, and route status and, when superseded, the earlier and current disposition.","ref":"Q-26"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"Destruction is recorded with a date, a quantity and a witness.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Collect destruction date, quantity, and witness for rejected stock, and prevent entry of a quantity greater than the displayed rejected quantity.","ref":"Q-27"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"Decisions waiting longer than 4 hours are escalated to the Quality Manager.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Identify decisions waiting more than four hours as escalated in the Quality Manager’s waiting-decisions view.","ref":"Q-28"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"A Quality Manager starts a recall for a product and one or more lot numbers, with a reason and a severity.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Provide a Quality Manager flow to start and close recalls with signed actions; recall start collects product, one or more lots, reason, and severity, and the app displays each returned action result.","ref":"Q-29"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"The trace from lot to every location and customer shall be available within one minute of the request.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Display the returned recall trace, including warehouse locations, boxes, routes, customer deliveries, quantities, delivery dates, receivers, and the trace total alongside received quantity when supplied.","ref":"Q-30"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"Notifies those customers by email and in the customer portal.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Show customer recall notices in the portal, link notices to affected deliveries, and provide a response entry point.","ref":"Q-31"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"The customer portal shows the organisation's orders, their status, the lots and expiry dates allocated, and for deliveries on the road the planned arrival time and whether the temperature is in range.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Show customers only their organisation’s current and past orders, allocated lots and expiry dates, order status, and in-transit delivery arrival and temperature status, without exposing other route customers.","ref":"Q-32"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"After delivery, the customer can download a delivery certificate as a PDF for each delivery.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Provide a PDF certificate for each completed delivery in the signed-in customer’s organisation, containing products, lots, expiry dates, quantities, receiver, handover time, each box’s temperature chart from sealing to handover, excursions, and signed excursion decisions.","ref":"Q-33"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"Each affected customer responds in the portal with, for each delivery, how many packs are still on hand, how many were used or dispensed, and how many were destroyed on site.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"When late readings produce a new certificate version, list the new and earlier versions for the signed-in customer’s completed delivery and keep each available for download.","ref":"Q-34"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"Recall progress shows the percentage of packs accounted for.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Present the customer portal and certificates in the user’s selected English or Arabic, render Arabic right to left including tables and charts, and show dates and times in the account’s configured time zone.","ref":"Q-35"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"A customer sees current and past orders of their own organisation only.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Provide an audit-trail screen showing returned entries with actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and supplied reason; support filters by record, user, date range, and action type, and export the filtered view.","ref":"Q-36"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"The certificate contains the contents by lot, the handover details, the temperature chart, and any excursions with their decisions.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Show the returned history of a lot from receipt through delivery or destruction in time order.","ref":"Q-37"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"The same figures shall be available on screen for any date range, filterable by warehouse.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Provide on-screen reports for selected date ranges and warehouses, with CSV export of displayed figures, covering excursion counts and rates by route, driver, vehicle, and shipper box type; packs rejected and destroyed by product and cause; on-time deliveries within 60 minutes of planned arrival and in-full deliveries when every ordered pack is handed over, each as a percentage; average time from excursion to decision; stock within 60 days of expiry by product and warehouse; and open recalls and their progress.","ref":"Q-38"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"The portal and the certificate are available in English and Arabic according to the user's preference.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Make the web app responsive on phone, tablet, and desktop browsers, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.","ref":"Q-39"},{"decision":"The request asks for it: \"The trace lists every warehouse location, box, route and customer delivery for the lot, with quantities.\"","how":"in-request","kind":"invented","problem":"Render the full recall trace returned by the service for the assumed launch scale.","ref":"Q-40"}],"spec":{"assumptions":["The responsive web app supports the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.","WCAG 2.1 AA applies to the main flows.","Launch scale is up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year.","Departure is blocked until every expected route box is scanned and wrong-route boxes are removed or corrected.","Unsent work affected by an offline route change remains available for review and resolution; completed handovers are preserved.","An offline handover completed despite a hold or recall conflict is retained, flagged, and associated with a quality case when synchronized.","Denied or unavailable browser location does not block a handover and is recorded as unavailable.","Live temperature, alert, box-association, and history data are supplied through an existing gateway API or feed.","A signer confirms identity using the sign-in method configured for that account.","Customer portal times use the user's configured account time zone.","Recall responses may leave a remainder unaccounted until later accounting or signed write-off.","Handover signatures and delivery photos are retained for seven years, matching audit-record retention.","A Quality Manager is authorized to sign a write-off.","Refusals are recorded by whole box, with a reason for each refused box.","One configured set of tier limits and allowances applies to all products.","Reports use on-screen date-range filters and CSV export; no custom report builder is included.","Quality-decision escalation and recall notices/reminders are email-only from fixed templates, with no SMS or push.","The customer portal and certificates support English and Arabic, including right-to-left Arabic layout.","The existing logger/gateway data and API/feed are supplied for consumption by the web app."],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"All pages render without horizontal scrolling at widths from 320 px through 1920 px; interactive touch targets on narrow viewports are at least 44 by 44 CSS px.","text":"The Meridian web app shall be responsive on phone, tablet, and desktop browsers, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"100% of primary driver and customer flow acceptance tests pass on the latest 2 released versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox.","text":"The Meridian web app shall support the latest two browser versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox."},{"id":"NFR-3","metric":"Automated accessibility checks report zero applicable WCAG 2.1 AA violations on main flows and manual keyboard checks pass.","text":"The main web-app flows shall conform to WCAG 2.1 AA."},{"id":"NFR-4","metric":"For responses containing up to 100,000 records, all returned trace entries are displayed or accessible within 60 seconds after the response is received.","text":"The web app shall render the full recall trace returned by the service for the assumed launch scale."},{"id":"NFR-5","metric":"With fixtures representing 1,000 users and 100,000 records, the trace screen displays the complete returned trace within 60 seconds of the user's request.","text":"The web client shall support the assumed first-year product scale and make a requested lot trace available through its screen within the requested time limit."}],"outOfScope":["API-side enforcement of credentials, password-reset token validity/delivery, role and access-scope authorization, and account state; web requirements cover forms, requests, screens, and API response handling.","API-side persistence and enforcement of stock/order/route transitions, hold and recall blocking across warehouses, quarantine, quantity validation/conservation, recall trace completeness and arithmetic, recall closure eligibility, write-off authorization, and duplicate-handover idempotency.","API-side audit creation, tamper detection, immutability, seven-year retention of audit records and handover evidence, and certificate-version persistence.","API-side scheduled and outbound emails, including recall notices and 24-hour reminders, four-hour decision escalation, daily summaries, monthly reports, and monthly report generation; web screens display supplied results/status where specified.","API-side production of recall traces within a time limit; the client timing requirements measure rendering after the response or from the user's request, as specified in separate requirements.","Supplying live temperature readings, alerts, box associations, and history through the existing logger or supplier gateway feed.","Importing or guaranteeing initial database contents; the web app provides opening-lot and stock entry.","Pricing, invoicing and payments; route stop-order optimization; manufacturer purchasing and demand forecasting; automatic driver or customer penalties; stock transfers between warehouses; logger hardware and supplier gateway implementation.","Native iOS or Android applications, app-store distribution, push notifications, and background location. The product is a responsive web app; applicable notices use in-app notices or email, location uses the browser prompt, and the web app may be installable."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user is on the sign-in page","id":"AC-1.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned sign-in result or error message","when":"the user submits an email address and password"},{"given":"A user is on the password-reset page","id":"AC-1.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned password-reset confirmation or error message","when":"the user submits an account email address"}],"ears":"The Meridian responsive web app shall provide individual email-and-password sign-in and self-service password reset for driver, staff, and customer areas.","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-1","I-1"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A System Administrator is viewing account management","id":"AC-2.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays account fields and the returned status or error message","when":"the administrator opens an account or submits account or access changes"},{"given":"A user without the System Administrator role opens account management","id":"AC-2.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays an access-denied message or the account-management page is not displayed","when":"the page loads"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall provide System Administrator screens to create and deactivate accounts and assign roles, staff warehouse access, and customer-organisation access.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-2","I-1"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Route data contains routes assigned to multiple drivers","id":"AC-3.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen lists only routes returned or assigned to that driver and displays each route's stops in order","when":"a driver opens today's route list"}],"ears":"When a driver opens today's routes, the Meridian web app shall show only that driver's assigned routes and each route's stops in route order.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-5","ASM-8","Q-2","I-1","I-2"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A route has an expected box that has not been scanned","id":"AC-4.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows the missing-box status and keeps the departure control unavailable","when":"the driver attempts to complete loading or depart"},{"given":"The driver scans a box assigned to another route","id":"AC-4.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows a wrong-route warning naming the box and keeps departure blocked","when":"the scan is processed"},{"given":"Every expected box is scanned and no wrong-route box remains","id":"AC-4.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows loading complete and displays an enabled departure control","when":"the driver completes loading"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall compare scanned shipper boxes with expected boxes before route departure, report missing or wrong-route boxes, and keep departure blocked until all expected boxes are scanned and wrong boxes are removed or corrected.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-8","I-2","I-10"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The route service returns stop statuses and update-time fields","id":"AC-5.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays each stop's returned status and last-updated time","when":"a dispatcher opens route monitoring"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall show dispatchers each route stop's status and last-updated time.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-5","ASM-9","I-9","I-10"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The gateway feed returns temperature, status, and alert data for route boxes","id":"AC-6.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays each box's current temperature, status, and returned alerts","when":"the driver opens route monitoring"},{"given":"The browser is disconnected and cached temperature data is available","id":"AC-6.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the cached temperature value and marks it stale","when":"the driver opens box monitoring"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall show each route box's latest available temperature, status, and alerts from the supplied gateway data and identify cached temperature data as stale while disconnected.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-12","I-3","I-21","I-42"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A stop includes a scanned box whose returned stock status is On Hold","id":"AC-7.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays “Do not deliver” and the hold reason and offers no enabled handover control for that box","when":"the driver opens that box's handover controls"},{"given":"A stop includes both On Hold and deliverable boxes","id":"AC-7.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen permits handover only for deliverable boxes","when":"the driver opens the handover screen"}],"ears":"When scanned stock is On Hold, the Meridian web app shall display “Do not deliver” and the returned hold reason and prevent handover of that box.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-1","ASM-10","I-4","I-11","I-14","I-16"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A driver is online and the service reports a scanned box as Recalled","id":"AC-8.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays “Do not deliver” and no enabled handover control for that box","when":"the driver opens that box's handover controls"},{"given":"The browser is offline and the cached status for a scanned box is Recalled","id":"AC-8.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays “Do not deliver” and no enabled handover control for that box","when":"the driver opens that box's handover controls"}],"ears":"When the service or an offline cache reports a scanned box as Recalled, the Meridian web app shall display “Do not deliver” and prevent handover of that box.","id":"REQ-8","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3","ASM-10"],"stability":0.6666666666666666},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A box is eligible for handover","id":"AC-9.1","level":"ui","then":"the handover request contains the receiver, signature, photo, actual completion time, and available location fields","when":"the driver enters the receiver name, captures a signature and photo, and completes handover"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall let drivers record an eligible handover with receiver name, signature, delivery photo, actual handover time, and available browser location.","id":"REQ-9","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-11","I-5","I-12","Q-4"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Browser location access is denied or unavailable","id":"AC-10.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the completed handover and a location-unavailable value, and the request records location as unavailable","when":"the driver completes an otherwise eligible handover"}],"ears":"If browser location is denied or unavailable, then the Meridian web app shall allow an otherwise eligible handover and record location as unavailable.","id":"REQ-10","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-11","I-5","I-12"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A driver is recording a refusal","id":"AC-11.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays each refused whole box with its reason and offers no partial-box quantity control","when":"the driver selects refused boxes and submits a reason for each"},{"given":"The service returns a refusal and quarantine result","id":"AC-11.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned refusal status and quarantine status for each refused box","when":"the driver opens the completed refusal"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall let drivers record full or partial refusal only by whole box and require a reason for each refused box.","id":"REQ-11","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-7","I-6","I-7"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The browser is offline","id":"AC-12.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows each action in the pending queue and retains its entered values","when":"the driver records loading, handover, or refusal work"},{"given":"Queued work exists and connectivity returns","id":"AC-12.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows queued work being sent without requiring resubmission, and displays the returned sync status","when":"the web app reconnects"},{"given":"A handover was recorded offline","id":"AC-12.3","level":"ui","then":"the request contains the original handover time and the same handover identifier as the original request","when":"the web app sends it or retries an interrupted send"},{"given":"Loading, handover, or refusal work, including handover signature and photo values, is queued while offline and the driver session expires or the driver signs out","id":"AC-12.4","level":"ui","then":"the screen lists the retained queued work and its entered values, and the request sends the work without requiring re-entry","when":"the driver re-authenticates and the connection returns"},{"given":"Driver A has queued work on a browser and Driver B signs in on that browser","id":"AC-12.5","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays no values from Driver A's queued work and no request sends Driver A's work under Driver B's account","when":"Driver B opens the pending-work view and connectivity returns"},{"given":"The service has acknowledged successful synchronization of queued work","id":"AC-12.6","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows no pending payload for that work and the request count for resending that work is zero","when":"the driver reloads the web app and connectivity returns again"},{"given":"The browser is offline and local storage cannot retain the complete payload for a loading, handover, or refusal action","id":"AC-12.7","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays a storage error, does not show the action as queued or completed, and the request count for sending that action is zero","when":"the driver attempts to save the action"},{"given":"The service permanently rejects queued work and returns an error","id":"AC-12.8","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned error and identifies the retained work as requiring review, the entered values remain available, and no automatic retry request is sent before user review","when":"the web app processes the synchronization response"},{"given":"Driver A has queued work, signs out, Driver B signs in on the same browser, and Driver A does not re-authenticate","id":"AC-12.9","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays no values from Driver A's queued work, the request count for sending Driver A's work is zero, and the queued work remains available after Driver A re-authenticates","when":"connectivity returns and Driver B opens the pending-work view"}],"ears":"While the browser is offline, the Meridian web app shall retain loading, handover, and refusal work locally across session expiry or sign-out, isolate queued work to the originating account so another signed-in user cannot view or send it, require the originating user to re-authenticate before syncing, automatically send queued work when connectivity returns, preserve handover occurrence time and identifier on retries, clear queued payload only after successful service acknowledgement, show an error without reporting work as queued when local storage cannot retain the complete payload, retain permanently rejected payloads and show the returned error while requiring user review before retry, and keep another account's queued payload inaccessible and unsent until the originating account re-authenticates.","id":"REQ-12","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-5","ASM-11","I-7","I-8","I-9","I-14","I-16"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The route returned after reconnection differs and unsent work exists","id":"AC-13.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen lists route differences and affected boxes requiring review","when":"the driver reconnects and the app reconciles the route"},{"given":"Route differences have unresolved affected boxes","id":"AC-13.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen blocks continuing and shows the unresolved boxes","when":"the driver attempts to continue route work"},{"given":"A handover was completed offline before the route changed","id":"AC-13.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen still displays the completed handover and its original time","when":"the new route is synchronized"}],"ears":"When an assigned route changes while a driver is offline, the Meridian web app shall show route differences, require review and resolution of affected unsent work before continuing, and preserve completed offline handovers.","id":"REQ-13","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-9","I-8","I-14","I-16"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An offline handover is synchronized and the service returns a hold or recall conflict and quality-case result","id":"AC-14.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the retained handover, conflict flag, and returned quality-case status","when":"the driver or quality user opens the synchronized record"}],"ears":"When an offline handover conflicts with a hold or recall upon synchronization, the Meridian web app shall retain and flag the handover and display the returned quality-case result.","id":"REQ-14","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-10","I-14","I-16","I-41","I-46","I-47"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An excursion review receives temperature history, tier budgets, and a recommendation","id":"AC-15.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the full history, used and remaining allowance for each tier, and the recommendation","when":"a Quality reviewer opens the affected handling unit"},{"given":"Configured tier limits and allowances are returned for different products","id":"AC-15.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the same configured tier-limit and allowance values for each product","when":"a user views settings or excursion reviews for those products"},{"given":"A signed-in user without excursion-review permission opens an excursion review and the service refuses access","id":"AC-15.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays an access-denied message and no excursion history, allowance values, or recommendation","when":"the review page loads"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall show Quality reviewers the full excursion temperature history, allowance used and remaining for each tier, and the returned recommendation, using the configured tier rules.","id":"REQ-15","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-8","ASM-12","I-21","I-22","I-23"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An excursion is within the first tier above or below the band, has allowance remaining, and the proposed decision matches the recommendation","id":"AC-16.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the single-person decision controls","when":"an eligible Quality Officer opens the decision form"},{"given":"An excursion is outside the single-person case or has no allowance remaining","id":"AC-16.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen requires a proposal and separate Quality Manager approval","when":"a Quality Officer opens the decision form"},{"given":"The proposing Quality Officer also has the Quality Manager role","id":"AC-16.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen does not offer an approval action to that same person","when":"that person attempts to approve the proposal"},{"given":"A proposed decision opposes the displayed recommendation, including for an excursion otherwise eligible for a single-person decision","id":"AC-16.4","level":"ui","then":"the screen requires a written-justification field, a Quality Officer proposal, and approval by a different Quality Manager","when":"a user prepares the decision"},{"given":"An excursion is within the first tier and has allowance remaining but the proposed decision opposes the recommendation","id":"AC-16.5","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the separate proposal and approval flow and does not display the single-person decision controls","when":"an eligible Quality Officer opens the decision form"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall present a single-person quality-decision flow only when an excursion is within the first tier above or below the permitted band, allowance remains, and the proposed decision matches the recommendation, and otherwise present a Quality Officer proposal and separate approval by a different Quality Manager; a written justification is required when a decision opposes the recommendation.","id":"REQ-16","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-13","I-24","I-25","I-26","I-27","I-28","I-29","I-30","I-31","I-32","I-33","Q-6"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user is ready to sign a quality decision","id":"AC-17.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen requires identity confirmation and a reason before showing the signed-decision status","when":"the user submits the signing form"},{"given":"A decision is returned as signed","id":"AC-17.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows signed values as read-only, provides a separate superseding-decision action, and offers no edit or delete control","when":"a user opens that decision"},{"given":"The service returns an earlier signed decision and a superseding decision","id":"AC-17.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays both signed decision records and identifies the superseding decision","when":"a reviewer opens decision history"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall require identity confirmation using the account's sign-in method and a reason when a user signs a quality decision, and present signed decisions as read-only with a separate superseding-decision action.","id":"REQ-17","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-1","ASM-13","I-25","I-33","I-34","I-35"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The service returns a release, rejection, or superseding disposition","id":"AC-18.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned stock, order, and route status and disposition history","when":"a Quality user views the affected stock or handling unit"},{"given":"The service rejects a superseding disposition because its reversal cannot be applied after stock was delivered or destroyed","id":"AC-18.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned error and unchanged returned stock, order, and route status, and does not present the superseding disposition as applied","when":"a Quality user views the affected stock or handling unit"}],"ears":"When the service returns a quality disposition, the Meridian web app shall show resulting stock, order, and route status and the earlier and current disposition when superseded.","id":"REQ-18","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-1","I-34","I-35","I-36"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A user opens destruction entry for rejected stock","id":"AC-19.1","level":"ui","then":"the request contains destruction date, quantity, and witness fields","when":"the user records destruction"},{"given":"The entered destruction quantity exceeds the displayed rejected quantity","id":"AC-19.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen shows a validation error and sends no destruction request","when":"the user submits the entry"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall collect destruction date, quantity, and witness for rejected stock and prevent entry of quantity greater than the displayed rejected quantity.","id":"REQ-19","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-36","I-37","I-38","ASM-1"],"stability":0.6666666666666666},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The service returns a decision waiting more than four hours as escalated","id":"AC-20.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen lists the decision and displays its escalated status","when":"a Quality Manager opens waiting decisions"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall identify quality decisions waiting more than four hours as escalated in the Quality Manager's waiting-decisions view.","id":"REQ-20","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-37","I-38","ASM-3","ASM-14"],"stability":0.3333333333333333},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A Quality Manager opens recall start","id":"AC-21.1","level":"ui","then":"the recall request contains those values and the screen displays the returned recall result","when":"the manager enters product, lot numbers, reason, severity, and signature"},{"given":"A Quality Manager closes a recall","id":"AC-21.2","level":"ui","then":"the close request contains the signature and the screen displays the returned close status or error message","when":"the manager submits the signed close action"},{"given":"A user who is not identified as eligible to manage recalls opens recall management","id":"AC-21.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen does not display recall start or close actions","when":"recall actions load"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall provide a Quality Manager flow to start and close recalls with signed actions, collecting product, one or more lots, reason, and severity for recall start, and display each returned action result.","id":"REQ-21","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3","Q-6","I-39","I-40","I-41","ASM-4"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A recall trace response contains affected locations and delivery records","id":"AC-22.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays each returned warehouse, box, route, customer delivery, quantity, delivery date, and receiver","when":"a Quality Manager opens the trace"},{"given":"The service returns trace quantities and the lot's total received quantity","id":"AC-22.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned trace total alongside the received quantity","when":"the user views the trace summary"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall display the returned recall trace, including warehouse locations, boxes, routes, customer deliveries, quantities, delivery dates, receivers, and the trace total alongside received quantity when supplied.","id":"REQ-22","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3","ASM-7","ASM-12","I-41","I-42","I-43"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The service returns an active recall notice for the signed-in customer's organisation","id":"AC-23.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the recall notice, its returned status, affected deliveries, and a response entry point","when":"the customer opens the portal"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall show customer recall notices in the portal, link notices to affected deliveries, and provide a response entry point.","id":"REQ-23","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-4","ASM-15","I-41","I-44"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A customer opens a recall response for a delivery","id":"AC-24.1","level":"ui","then":"the response request contains the entered quantity fields for that delivery","when":"the customer enters on-hand, used or dispensed, and destroyed quantities"},{"given":"The reported quantities total less than the delivered quantity","id":"AC-24.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen accepts the values and displays the difference as unaccounted quantity","when":"the customer submits the response"},{"given":"The reported quantities exceed the delivered quantity","id":"AC-24.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays a validation error or returned error message and sends no invalid response request","when":"the customer submits the response"},{"given":"A previously submitted response has an unaccounted remainder","id":"AC-24.4","level":"ui","then":"the request identifies that delivery and contains the updated quantity fields, and the screen displays the returned response and remaining unaccounted quantity","when":"the customer adds or revises the quantities for that delivery and submits the update"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall let customers submit or update per-delivery on-hand, used or dispensed, and destroyed quantities, allow a total below the delivered amount as unaccounted, and reject a total above it.","id":"REQ-24","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3","I-41","I-45","I-46"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The service returns recall progress and outstanding customers","id":"AC-25.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the accounted percentage and outstanding-customer list","when":"a Quality Manager opens recall progress"},{"given":"The service returns customer response and reminder statuses","id":"AC-25.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned reminder status","when":"a user opens recall progress"},{"given":"A Quality Manager selects unaccounted quantity for write-off","id":"AC-25.3","level":"ui","then":"the request contains a signed justification and the screen displays the returned write-off status or refusal message","when":"the manager submits the write-off"},{"given":"A recall has unaccounted quantity without a signed write-off","id":"AC-25.4","level":"ui","then":"the screen blocks submission and displays the outstanding quantity or returned close error","when":"a Quality Manager attempts to close the recall"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall show recall progress as the returned percentage accounted for, identify outstanding customers and reminder status when supplied, and let a Quality Manager submit a signed write-off justification for unaccounted quantity.","id":"REQ-25","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-3","Q-6","ASM-15","I-41","I-46","I-47"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A signed-in customer belongs to one organisation and the service provides an authenticated, organisation-scoped response despite having records for other organisations","id":"AC-26.1","level":"ui","then":"the request contains no caller-supplied identifier for another organisation and the screen lists only the signed-in organisation's returned orders, status, lots, and expiry dates","when":"the customer opens the orders page"},{"given":"The service returns an in-transit delivery with arrival and temperature status","id":"AC-26.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays planned arrival and in-range or out-of-range status and no other customer's identity or delivery details","when":"the customer views the delivery"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall show customers only their organisation's current and past orders, allocated lots and expiry dates, order status, and in-transit delivery arrival and temperature status, without exposing other route customers.","id":"REQ-26","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-2","ASM-16","ASM-17","I-48","I-49","I-50"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A completed delivery in the signed-in customer's organisation has a certificate available","id":"AC-27.1","level":"ui","then":"the downloaded file is a PDF containing the listed delivery, handover, temperature, excursion, and decision fields","when":"the customer selects certificate download"},{"given":"A customer belongs to Organisation A and a delivery belongs to Organisation B","id":"AC-27.2","level":"ui","then":"the service response status is 403 or 404, the screen displays an access-denied or not-found message, and no certificate file or download link is displayed","when":"the customer changes the delivery identifier in a certificate URL to Organisation B's delivery"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall provide a PDF certificate for each completed delivery in the signed-in customer's organisation with products, lots, expiry dates, quantities, receiver, handover time, each box's temperature chart from sealing to handover, excursions, and signed excursion decisions.","id":"REQ-27","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-4","ASM-16","ASM-18","I-50"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The service returns a new certificate version and retains the earlier version","id":"AC-28.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen lists both versions and provides a file download link for each","when":"the customer opens certificate history"},{"given":"A customer belongs to Organisation A and a certificate history belongs to Organisation B","id":"AC-28.2","level":"ui","then":"the service response status is 403 or 404, the screen lists no certificate versions, and no download links are displayed","when":"the customer opens Organisation B's certificate-history URL"}],"ears":"When late readings produce a new certificate version, the Meridian web app shall list the new and earlier versions for the signed-in customer's completed delivery and keep each available for download.","id":"REQ-28","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-4","ASM-18"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The user selects Arabic","id":"AC-29.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen and certificate display Arabic content with right-to-left direction for tables and charts","when":"the portal and a delivery certificate are displayed"},{"given":"The user's account has a configured time zone","id":"AC-29.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the values in that configured time zone","when":"the portal displays order or delivery dates and times"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall present the customer portal and certificates in the user's selected English or Arabic, render Arabic right to left including tables and charts, and show dates and times in the account's configured time zone.","id":"REQ-29","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-6","ASM-16","ASM-18","I-13","I-15","I-17","I-18","I-19","I-20","I-50"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"Audit entries are returned for multiple records, users, dates, and action types","id":"AC-30.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays each entry's actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and supplied reason","when":"an Auditor opens the audit trail"},{"given":"An Auditor selects audit filters","id":"AC-30.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the matching returned list and provides a file containing the filtered view","when":"the filters are applied and the Auditor exports the view"},{"given":"A signed-in user without audit-trail permission opens the audit trail and the service refuses access","id":"AC-30.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays an access-denied message and no audit entries, filters, or export action","when":"the audit-trail page loads"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall provide an audit-trail screen showing returned entries with actor, time, changed fields, old and new values, and supplied reason, with filters by record, user, date range, and action type and export of the filtered view.","id":"REQ-30","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-4","I-13","I-15","I-17","I-18","I-19","I-20"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A lot-history response contains receipt, movement, delivery, or destruction events","id":"AC-31.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the returned events in time order","when":"an Auditor opens lot history"},{"given":"A signed-in user without lot-history permission opens a lot history and the service refuses access","id":"AC-31.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays an access-denied message and no lot-history events","when":"the lot-history page loads"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall show the returned history of a lot from receipt through delivery or destruction in time order.","id":"REQ-31","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-4","Q-5","ASM-1"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"The service returns report figures for a selected date range and warehouse","id":"AC-32.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays returned excursion counts and rates by route, driver, vehicle, and shipper box type; packs rejected and destroyed by product and cause; on-time delivery and in-full percentages; average time from excursion to decision; stock within 60 days of expiry by product and warehouse; and open recalls and their progress","when":"staff open the reports screen"},{"given":"A staff user has warehouse access scope","id":"AC-32.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen offers only in-scope warehouses and the downloaded CSV file contains the displayed filtered figures","when":"the user filters reports and exports them"},{"given":"A signed-in user without report access opens the reports page and the service refuses access","id":"AC-32.3","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays an access-denied message and no report figures or export action","when":"the page loads"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall provide on-screen reports for selected date ranges and warehouses, with CSV export of displayed figures, including excursion counts and rates by route, driver, vehicle, and shipper box type; packs rejected and destroyed by product and cause; deliveries on time within 60 minutes of planned arrival and in full when every ordered pack is handed over, each as a percentage; average time from excursion to decision; stock within 60 days of expiry by product and warehouse; and open recalls and their progress.","id":"REQ-32","op":"ADDED","sources":["ASM-2","ASM-15","I-50"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"An authorized staff user opens opening-inventory entry","id":"AC-33.1","level":"ui","then":"the request contains the entered opening lot and stock fields and the screen displays the returned result or error","when":"the user enters lot and stock details"},{"given":"A signed-in user without opening-inventory permission opens opening-inventory entry and the service refuses access","id":"AC-33.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays an access-denied message and no opening-inventory form or records","when":"the page loads"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall provide forms to enter opening lots and stock records and submit them to the service.","id":"REQ-33","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-20","Q-5"],"stability":0.6666666666666666},{"acceptance":[{"given":"A delivery record within its retention period includes signature and photo evidence","id":"AC-34.1","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays the signature and photo fields or their available file links","when":"an authorized user opens the delivery record"},{"given":"A signed-in user without delivery-evidence permission opens a delivery record and the service refuses access","id":"AC-34.2","level":"ui","then":"the screen displays an access-denied message and no signature, photo, or evidence file links","when":"the evidence view loads"}],"ears":"The Meridian web app shall make recorded handover signatures and delivery photos available from a delivery record within its seven-year evidence-retention period.","id":"REQ-34","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-4"],"stability":1}]}}